---
description: Use for plain Node.js backend projects (package.json present, no react/react-native/@angular/core dependency) — Promact best practices and coding guidelines for Node.js
globs:
alwaysApply: false
---

Node.js has no reliable glob signature of its own (a `package.json` alone
doesn't distinguish it from React/Angular/React Native) — check the
project's `package.json` dependencies first. If it has no `react`,
`react-native`, or `@angular/core` dependency, apply Promact's Node.js
conventions below when writing or reviewing code.

@../../skills/best-practices/stacks/nodejs.md
@../../skills/coding-guidelines/stacks/nodejs.md

For cross-cutting concerns (REST API design, exception handling, security,
database access, naming, code organization, testing structure), see the
other rules in this directory — they apply regardless of stack.
